    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-09T04:10:48+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-09T04:10:48+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-08T17:40:48Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-08T17:40:48Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough and cold front over western SA will track eastwards across the rest of SA on Friday before a weak high briefly establishes in the north on Saturday. Another series of troughs and cold fronts are expected to enter western SA early on Sunday, crossing the state then clearing in the east by the end of Monday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW012" description="Lower Eyre Peninsula" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-09T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-10T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-08T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-09T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers, becoming less likely late this afternoon and evening. A thunderstorm likely during the morning and afternoon, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding. Winds north to northwesterly 25 to 35 km/h turning westerly 25 to 40 km/h in the early afternoon. Daytime maximum temperatures in the low 20s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">No Rating</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 10:00am to 4:20pm, UV Index predicted to reach 7 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-10T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-11T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-09T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-10T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower in the morning and afternoon. Winds westerly 25 to 35 km/h becoming light in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny morning. Slight chance of a shower in the afternoon and evening. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Thunderstorms possibly severe with damaging winds near the west coast in the evening. Winds northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h turning northwesterly 25 to 40 km/h during the afternoon then tending westerly 15 to 25 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-12T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-13T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-11T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-12T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower, most likely in the morning. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning. Winds westerly 15 to 25 km/h tending southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to around 11 with daytime temperatures reaching around 18.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
